Falsifies `globally_unique_identifier_partition_table::verification::the_header_crc_in_pieces_is_the_crc_of_the_whole`.

The defect: each piece restarts the running CRC from its initial value, so the CRC of a header taken
in three pieces (before the CRC field, the field read as zero, after it) is the CRC of the last
piece alone. Every header this crate writes or checks would carry a CRC that covers only its tail.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(crc::crc32_pieces(&pieces), whole)`, on any input whose cuts
leave a nonempty piece before a later one.
diff --git a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
index 9d40df3d1..b39714c2a 100644
--- a/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
+++ b/crates/globally_unique_identifier_partition_table/src/crc.rs
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ pub fn crc32(bytes: &[u8]) -> u32 {
 pub(crate) fn crc32_pieces(pieces: &[&[u8]]) -> u32 {
     let mut crc = !0u32;
     for piece in pieces {
-        crc = update(crc, piece);
+        crc = update(!0u32, piece);
     }
     !crc
 }
